extraction_notes: |
  - Transcribed from printed 77-79 (cache p078-p080); the bonus lines, the
    skill list and the XP ladder were read off renders. The ladder is the
    "Mystic Knight, Lord Magus" column on printed 160, shared with the Mystic
    Knight; xp_table holds each band''s lower bound. Its level-15 cell prints
    350,601425,800 with the hyphen dropped, and the lower bound 350,601 is
    stored.
  - Initial spells: "all spells of illusion regardless of level, and all spell
    incantations from levels 1-2". The catalog carries no school, so both sets
    are named lists, drawn on 2026-09-26 from production: every general
    invocation (no tradition) of spell level 1-2 available to Rifts, and the
    eleven general invocations whose own descriptions call them illusions.
    Spells imported later at those levels are not added by themselves.
  - Schedule counts printed as dice (1D6+4, 1D4+4, 1D4+3, 1D4+2) store the
    maximum and tell the player to roll, the convention the Lanotaur Hunter set.
    "At level six on up ... one new spell from levels 8-10, or two from levels
    3-7" is read as per level; each entry offers two picks from levels 3-10 and
    its note carries the either/or, which the catalog cannot enforce.
  - The creature-of-magic progression is level_progression prose. Nothing here
    changes the sheet at level 8 (M.D.C. conversion) or level 13
    (supernatural P.S.), and the level-4 P.P.E. increase of 6D6+20 is not
    added to ppe_base: an at_level pool is not applied.
  - "+2 to save vs illusions" is illusionary_magic. "Impervious to possession"
    (level 5) and "impervious to illusions" (level 14) have no save key and
    stay prose.
  - The abilities section opens "although the High Magus has minimal physical
    bonuses", a sentence repeated from the High Magus; it is not transcribed.
  - Interrogation (+10%) is the Espionage row Interrogation.
  - The body armor (50 M.D.C.) and helmet (45 M.D.C.), the magical staff (2D6
    M.D.) and the two other magic weapons have no catalog rows and stay in the
    Equipment section. A half dozen pens or markers is six pens.
  - men_of_arms is false: the book files the class under its "Magus O.C.C.s"
    heading (printed 70), a school of magic.
---

## Lore

The Lord Magus takes "one with magic" to the extreme. Ten to twelve years of study and alien meditation techniques, known only to the Lords of Magic and the Brotherhood of Magic, slowly transform him into a creature of magic, much as dragons and Faerie Folk are, on a less primal level. He feels detached from mortals and would rather study magic and its nature than anything else, so the spells he knows at first level are most of what he will ever learn; most stop searching for new incantations by 6th level.

The Lord Magi are the elite spell casters of Dweomer: teachers of magic, administrators, heads of state and, in a military context, officers from Captains to Generals. For every fifty Battle Magi there is one Lord Magus. They make excellent explorers and champions against great evil and the supernatural.

Alignment: any; most are Scrupulous, Unprincipled, Anarchist, Miscreant or Aberrant.

## Equipment

Clothes, uniform, ceremonial robes, utility belt, a canteen, backpack, knapsack, duffle bag, three small sacks, magnifying glass, binoculars, notebook, a half dozen pens or markers, portable disk recorder, a flashlight, compass and pocket knife.

Standard Lord Magus body armor (50 M.D.C.) and helmet (45 M.D.C.), insect or crustacean in appearance with a long segmented hood; the fingers are tipped with spike-like claws (+1D6 S.D.C. to damage, M.D.C. when combined with Fist of Fury or Power Weapon). Not a full environmental suit.

Weapons: a magical staff (2D6 M.D.) and two other magic weapons of choice, made by the Magi or by Techno-Wizards.

Money: as an elite member of the Dweomer Defense Force he has a roomy four-bedroom apartment, meals, uniforms, healing and access to the laboratories and academies, with a monthly salary of 3000 credits. Starts with 2D6x1,000 Universal Credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'lord-magus');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'lord-magus';

